          <msContents>
            <summary>This medical manuscript is a copy of the Viaticum. 
              The manuscript has used a possibly 14th century manuscript as part of the binding. This has not been identified but it appears to be from a work on the Monastic Constitution of Evesham.
              It is written in double columns of 31 lines, with extensive marginal glosses by contemporary and later hands. It has initials in alternate red and blue, and blue and red. 
            </summary>
            <textLang mainLang="la" source="IANA">Latin</textLang>
            <msItem n="1" xml:id="MS_209_1">
              <author>Constantinus Afircans, cc. 1087</author>
              <title type="original">Viaticum</title>
              <textLang mainLang="la" source="IANA">Latin</textLang>
              <incipit>
                Quoniam quidem ut in rethoricis tullius ['omne' superscribed] inquit expetendum... 
              </incipit>
              <explicit>
                Fol. 120v Capillus ex fumo grosso... 
                line 25 ...ad idem valent. 
                Conclee marine incense/cum olio rosato multum valent
              </explicit>
            </msItem>
          </msContents>
