            <additions>
              Above the text on fol. 1, a 16th cent. hand has written 'Constantini Affricani Monast[erii] Casanensis Viaticum. Agit de morbis et eorum signis et remediis'. 
            </additions>
            <bindingDesc>
              <binding>
                <p>Original rough calf binding, with two leather and metal clasps.</p>
                <p>The fly-leaves, two at each end of which one is pasted down in to each cover, are folio leaves (cut down) from a 14th cent. MS. </p>
              </binding>
